      "exam_answer_md": "First differences (5, 7, 9, 12, 14, 17) are not constant; second differences are nearly constant (about 2 to 3), so a **quadratic trend** S = a + bt + ct² is appropriate. Code t = -3 to 3 with 1993 = 0 so that the sum of t is 0."
