    {
      "id": "be-s9-trend-c3",
      "heading": "Fitting the quadratic trend",
      "explanation_md": "With the sums from the table (sum of S = 252, sum of t² = 28, sum of t⁴ = 196, sum of St = 297, sum of St² = 1109), the equations are:\n\n- 252 = 7a + 28c\n- 297 = 28b\n- 1109 = 28a + 196c\n\n| Unknown | Working | Value |\n|---|---|---|\n| b | 297 / 28 | **10.607** |\n| c | from the first and third equations | **1.202** |\n| a | from 252 = 7a + 28c | **31.19** |\n\nThe slide prints b = 10.067, but 297 / 28 is **10.607**.\n\nThe year 2000 is **t = 7** (1996 is t = 3). Forecast: 31.19 + 10.607 x 7 + 1.202 x 49 = **164.36**. The slide's 160.56 comes from its typo in b.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Quadratic trend S = 31.19 + 10.607t + 1.202t²; forecast for 2000 (t = 7) is 164.36.",
      "clarification": null,
